            <article class="acnn-rdp-lab reveal">
                <div class="acnn-rdp-lab-txt"><span class="no">08</span><small>Electrical properties of materials</small><h3>Electrical Measurement Lab</h3><p>For measurement of electrical properties of materials for applications in transformer cores, high-frequency applications and other areas of electrical engineering and technology.</p><ul class="acnn-rdp-tags"><li>Precision Multiferroic Test System (P-E, piezoelectric, magneto-electric; temperature variation)</li><li>Impedance Analyser</li><li>Make: Radiant Technologies Inc., USA</li></ul><div class="acnn-rdp-note"><i class="icon-lightbulb"></i><p>Dielectric measurements in the 100 Hz–1 MHz range show that these substituted ferrites have low dielectric loss, suitable for high-frequency applications (R.K. Singh et al., Materials Science and Engineering B 210, 2016, 64–69).</p></div></div>
                <div class="acnn-rdp-lab-ph n3"><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p012_054.jpg" title="Electrical Measurement Lab"><img src="img/rd/p012_054.jpg" alt="Electrical Measurement Lab" loading="lazy" /></a><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p012_055.jpg" title="Electrical Measurement Lab"><img src="img/rd/p012_055.jpg" alt="Electrical Measurement Lab" loading="lazy" /></a><a class="acnn-rdp-ph  fit" href="img/rd/p012_056.jpg" title="Electrical Measurement Lab"><img src="img/rd/p012_056.jpg" alt="Electrical Measurement Lab" loading="lazy" /></a></div>
