    <section id="rd-outreach" class="acnn-rdp-sec">
        <div class="acnn-rdp-head reveal"><span class="acnn-about-tag">Outreach</span><h2>Anveshika — A Laboratory for All</h2><p>An initiative of Padma Shri Prof. H.C. Verma, Dept. of Physics, IIT Kanpur</p></div>
        <div class="acnn-rdp-two">
            <article class="acnn-rdp-card reveal">
                <h3>Anveshika Activities</h3>
                <p class="lead">Natural process of learning through low-cost experiments &mdash; inspiring innovation at all levels of study. An open laboratory to nurture young minds.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Impact:</b> these experiments have been demonstrated in regular classrooms and special lecture sessions and, when combined with the right type of questions, are very effective tools for concept-building and interest generation in basic science and interdisciplinary scientific research.</li>
                    <li>About <b>25 teachers and 100 students</b> came into close contact and are working for science education and research. Such activity also fosters growth in higher education.</li>
                    <li>A low-cost science-learning laboratory was established as a community science centre.</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="acnn-rdp-ph3"><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p015_066.jpg" title="Anveshika demonstration"><img src="img/rd/p015_066.jpg" alt="Anveshika demonstration" loading="lazy" /></a><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p015_067.jpg" title="Senior Resource Persons meet"><img src="img/rd/p015_067.jpg" alt="Senior Resource Persons meet" loading="lazy" /></a><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p015_068.jpg" title="Lecture session"><img src="img/rd/p015_068.jpg" alt="Lecture session" loading="lazy" /></a></div>
            </article>
            <article class="acnn-rdp-card reveal">
                <h3>NAEST &mdash; Best Practice</h3>
                <p class="lead">National Anveshika Experimental Skill Test: research-driven learning, uplifting science education and related innovations at all levels of study.</p>
                <p>Experiments are an integral part of science. To promote these skills among students, the National Anveshika Network of India (NANI), a unit of the Indian Association of Physics Teachers, conducts NAEST every year since 2014 &mdash; probably the only test of its kind in India.</p>
                <p>In the <b>Screening Round</b>, 8&ndash;10 short videos of innovative experiments related to natural phenomena are shown and observation skills are tested. Selected students go to the <b>Prelims Round</b>, conducted by the 26 Anveshikas across the country, which focuses on performing experiments and analysing data. These activities have been carried out for the last 12 years across the nation.</p>
                <div class="acnn-rdp-ph2"><a class="acnn-rdp-ph  fit" href="img/rd/p016_069.jpg" title="NAEST 2020 Certificate of Appreciation"><img src="img/rd/p016_069.jpg" alt="NAEST 2020 Certificate of Appreciation" loading="lazy" /></a><a class="acnn-rdp-ph " href="img/rd/p016_070.jpg" title="Seminar on World Year of Physics"><img src="img/rd/p016_070.jpg" alt="Seminar on World Year of Physics" loading="lazy" /></a></div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>


    <section id="rd-collab" class="acnn-rdp-sec">
        <div class="acnn-rdp-head reveal"><span class="acnn-about-tag">Collaboration</span><h2>Achievements at National / International Level</h2><p>National linkage of faculty and research scholars for promoting and sharing teaching and research programmes</p></div>
        <ul class="acnn-rdp-inst reveal"><li>Nalanda University, Rajgir</li><li>Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur</li><li>School of Materials Science &amp; Technology, IIT (BHU), Varanasi</li><li>Indian Institute of Technology, Patna</li><li>Magnetic Measurement Laboratory, National Physical Laboratory, New Delhi</li><li>Dept. of Physics &amp; Ferroelectric Material Research Centre, A.N. College, Patna</li><li>P.G. Department of Physics, Patna University, Patna</li><li>Inter-University Accelerator Centre (IUAC), New Delhi</li><li>Indian Institute of Information Technology and Management (IITM), Jabalpur</li><li>VTU Bangalore and RMRI Patna</li></ul>
        <div class="acnn-rdp-call reveal">
            <h3>Require potential collaborators / support for R &amp; D activities</h3>
            <p>The Centre has all 6 advanced materials science and nanotechnology laboratories. For sustainability, support for AMC and maintenance is urgently required.</p>
            <p>Production of silica nanomaterials from agricultural waste (rice husk), eco-friendly production of ceramic magnetic nanomaterials, evidence-based Ayurvedic nanomedicine and food materials are possible for <b>Atmanirbhar Bharat</b>. Help of potential industry partners is required.</p>
        </div>
